{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Git Github - mod-5\n\n",
        "**Course:** git-github\n\n",
        "Run the code cells below to practice.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "bash",
          "# List your remotes\ngit remote -v\n# origin  git@github.com:user/repo.git (fetch)\n# origin  git@github.com:user/repo.git (push)\n\n# Show details about a remote\ngit remote show origin"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "bash",
          "# Add a remote\ngit remote add origin git@github.com:user/repo.git\n\n# Add a second remote (e.g., a mirror on GitLab)\ngit remote add gitlab git@gitlab.com:user/repo.git\n\n# Rename / remove\ngit remote rename origin upstream\ngit remote remove gitlab\n\n# Change a remote's URL (e.g., switch HTTPS \u2192 SSH)\ngit remote set-url origin git@github.com:user/repo.git"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "bash",
          "# First push of a new branch \u2014 sets up tracking with -u\ngit push -u origin main\n\n# After tracking is set, just:\ngit push\n\n# Push a specific branch\ngit push origin feature-login\n\n# Push all branches\ngit push --all origin\n\n# Push tags\ngit push --tags"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "bash",
          "# Safe: download, then look before you leap\ngit fetch origin\ngit log HEAD..origin/main --oneline   # what's new on the remote?\ngit merge origin/main                  # integrate when ready\n\n# Convenient: fetch + merge in one command\ngit pull\n\n# Fetch + rebase instead of merge (linear history)\ngit pull --rebase"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "bash",
          "# See tracking relationships\ngit branch -vv\n# * main  a1b2c3d [origin/main] Latest commit message\n\n# Set upstream for an existing branch\ngit branch --set-upstream-to=origin/main"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "bash",
          "# 1. Start your day \u2014 get the latest\ngit switch main\ngit pull --rebase\n\n# 2. Create a feature branch\ngit switch -c feature-search\n\n# 3. Work and commit\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"Add search endpoint\"\n\n# 4. Push your branch\ngit push -u origin feature-search\n\n# 5. Open a Pull/Merge Request on the host (covered next module)\n\n# 6. After it merges, clean up\ngit switch main\ngit pull --rebase\ngit branch -d feature-search"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "bash",
          "git remote add upstream git@github.com:original-owner/repo.git\n\n# Get their latest changes\ngit fetch upstream\ngit switch main\ngit merge upstream/main      # or: git rebase upstream/main\ngit push origin main         # update your fork"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "bash",
          "git push\n# ! [rejected] main -> main (fetch first)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "bash",
          "git pull --rebase\n# resolve any conflicts, then:\ngit push"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "bash",
          "git push --force-with-lease"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
